WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.920
A heavy crate is hard to get moving.

2
00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.340
Its mass resists any change in its motion.

3
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:11.750
Spinning has a twin of mass: a
resistance to any change in rotation.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.170
Now take a hoop and a solid wheel.

5
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.150
Same mass.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.560
Same radius.

7
00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.230
Each on its own axle through the middle.

8
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.300
Give each the same twist.

9
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:25.870
Do they spin up equally fast, or
is one harder to start spinning?

10
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.040
In this mission, you'll add up this
resistance for small masses fixed along a

11
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.330
light rod.

12
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.660
Then you'll compare hoops,
solid wheels and rods,

13
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.210
each turning about a chosen axis.

14
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.710
Your mission: decide which
is harder to start spinning,

15
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:41.950
and explain why.
